# Brunnwinkl bee house (Bienenhaus, back layer, D-031): an open wooden shed,
# wood o/O/l, three shelves of hive boxes in two bays, each box front a small
# painted 8x5 folk-art panel (Bienenstock-Stirnbrett: heart, tree, flower,
# house, hills, tulip in R/G/O on c/p/t fields, no text) with its flight slit
# and O landing board; dark l shelves; plank wall and an i/m stone footing below. Its roof is the
# level's roof_shingle tiles on top (5 tiles up), so the beam ends at row 0.
# No k, no outline (back layer). Drawn by the pixel-artist with a throwaway
# script; the grid below is the source.
sprite = bienenhaus
size   = 128x80
origin = 64,80
anim   = idle frames=1
---
frame idle 0
